   "body": "If a `remove()` call throws, `deletedAll.set(true)` is skipped. The non-daemon reader thread then loops forever and can hang the test JVM. On the success path the test also asserts without joining the thread. A request still in flight can fail after the assertion, and that failure is missed. Wrap the deletes in try/finally that sets the flag. Keep a reference to the thread, join it before asserting, and consider making it a daemon."
